# Task 1: base terminology (races, classes). Attribute names (Strength,
# Intelligence, Wisdom, Dexterity, Constitution, Charisma) are already
# covered via the item-name matching below (they're also potion/ring
# names in data_treasure.cpp, e.g. "Potion of Strength"), reusing
# Hengband's terms (e.g. Strength -> "腕力") rather than jmoria's
# (筋力/器用度/体力), consistent with the phase 5 decision to prefer
# Hengband's vocabulary. Race/class names below are from Hengband's
# src/player/race-info-table.cpp and src/player-info/class-info.cpp.
#
# Note: Umoria's race is named "Halfling" (data_player.cpp) while
# Hengband's equivalent race is named "Hobbit" (an old vs. new Angband
# naming difference, likely a Tolkien-trademark rename upstream at some
# point) -- same race concept, so Hengband's Japanese term for it
# ("ホビット") is reused for Umoria's "Halfling" msgid. Flagged for
# review since the English labels don't match even though the race is
# the same.
# Half-Elf/Half-Orc/Half-Troll: Hengband's own terms are the fuller
# katakana forms (ハーフエルフ/ハーフオーク/ハーフトロル), but those hit
# exactly the 15-display-column width of character.cpp's race-selection
# grid slot (coord.x += 15 per entry, not displayWidth-aware -- a known
# display-width limitation of that fixed-column layout), leaving zero visual gap before the
# next entry. Shortened to the kanji+katakana hybrid forms below
# (matching jmoria's original vocabulary for these three races) so the
# grid keeps a comfortable margin. This is a UI-layout-driven exception
# to the "prefer Hengband" policy, not a reversal of it.
msgid "Half-Elf"
msgstr "半エルフ"

msgid "Elf"
msgstr "エルフ"

msgid "Halfling"
msgstr "ホビット"

